Defines all physical and virtual places where stock is stored, moved, or counted — the backbone of Odoo’s inventory and warehouse structure.
Key Functional Use Cases:

Warehouse structure (WH/Stock, WH/Stock/Shelf01, etc.)
Internal locations, supplier/customer locations, inventory loss, production, transit
Multi-warehouse and multi-step routing (MTO, dropship, cross-dock)
Stock valuation and accounting (valuation accounts per location)
Putaway, removal, and replenishment strategies
Physical inventory counts and cycle counts
Scrap, production, and quality control locations

Technical DNA:

Model Type: models.Model (persistent)
Key Fields:
name (char, required), complete_name (computed)
location_id → stock.location (parent, hierarchical)
usage (selection: internal, customer, supplier, inventory, production, transit, view)
company_id, warehouse_id → stock.warehouse
active, scrap_location, return_location
property_stock_valuation_account_id, property_stock_account_input, property_stock_account_output
removal_strategy_id (FIFO/LIFO/FEFO), putaway_strategy_ids

Critical Hooks: _compute_complete_name, _check_location_recursion, onchange_company_id
Security: stock.group_stock_manager + company + location-based record rules

RAG Routing Keywords:
stock location, inventory location, warehouse location, internal location, stock shelf, stock bin, storage location, customer location, supplier location, transit location, virtual location, stock.warehouse location, putaway location
Related Models (most joined):

stock.warehouse (via warehouse_id)
stock.quant (stock levels per location)
stock.move (location_id, location_dest_id)
stock.picking
product.product (via quants)
stock.location.route
stock.rule

Ultra-Dense Vector Paragraph:
stock.location is Odoo’s hierarchical model defining every storage place with usage (internal/customer/supplier/production/transit), parent location, warehouse, valuation accounts, and strategies. It controls stock movements (stock.move), real-time quantities (stock.quant), putaway/removal logic, multi-warehouse operations, and accounting postings across Inventory, Manufacturing, Sales, and Purchase modules.